Now automove.js. Need careful event sequences and promotion. Let's write.

Important: `core.squareCenter(index, rect, orientation)` returns `{x,y,cell}`. Good.

`clickPoint` uses `document.elementFromPoint`; if the point is outside viewport, coordinates might be negative. Check.

`fire`:
```js
function fire(target, type, x, y, buttons, opts) {
  var init = { bubbles:true, cancelable:true, composed:true, view: window, clientX:x, clientY:y, screenX:x + (window.screenX||0), screenY:... , button:0, buttons:buttons, detail: type==='click'?1:0 };
  var event;
  try {
    if (window.PointerEvent && type.indexOf('pointer') === 0) {
      init.pointerId = 1; init.pointerType='mouse'; init.isPrimary=true; init.width=1; init.height=1; init.pressure = buttons ? 0.5 : 0;
      event = new PointerEvent(type, init);
    } else {
      event = new MouseEvent(type, init);
    }
  } catch (e) { ... }
  target.dispatchEvent(event);
}
```
- For `pointermove`, `pressure` 0.5; `tiltX` etc. not needed.
- Need `button` for mousemove = 0; `buttons` 1.
- `which`? Some libs read `which`; MouseEvent init doesn't support `which` (read-only). Legacy sites might use `event.which`; not much we can do; could define property after creation:
```js
try { Object.defineProperty(event, 'which', {value: type==='mousedown'||...?1:0}); } catch {}
```
Not necessary.
- `target` may be `document` or `window`. `dispatchEvent` works on window? Window is an EventTarget; yes. But we target board/element.

`clickPoint`:
```js
async function clickPoint(boardEl, x, y, orientation) {
  var el = document.elementFromPoint(x,y) || boardEl;
  // ensure target is inside the board? If the board is in an iframe, coordinates are fine; content script top-level only.
  fire(el, 'pointerover', x,y,0);
  fire(el, 'pointerenter', x,y,0); // pointerenter doesn't bubble; fine
  fire(el, 'mousemove', x,y,0);
  fire(el, 'pointerdown', x,y,1);
  fire(el, 'mousedown', x,y,1);
  await sleep(22);
  fire(el, 'pointerup', x,y,0);
  fire(el, 'mouseup', x,y,0);
  fire(el, 'click', x,y,0);
}
```
- `pointerenter` not bubbling; dispatch on target still triggers listeners on target.
- If the element is a text node? elementFromPoint returns Element.
- For chess.com, `pointerdown` may trigger a drag mode; then `pointerup` immediately triggers a click-select. Good.
- Some sites use `mousedown` with `event.buttons` and then `mouseup` on `document`. Our event bubbles to document. Good.
- Add `window.focus()`? Not needed.

`drag`:
```js
async function drag(boardEl, from, to) {
  var target = boardEl;
  fire(target,'pointerover',from.x,from.y,0);
  fire(target,'mousemove',from.x,from.y,0);
  fire(target,'pointerdown',from.x,from.y,1);
  fire(target,'mousedown',from.x,from.y,1);
  await 30;
  var steps=6;
  for ... { fire(target,'pointermove',...1); fire(target,'mousemove',...1); await 16; }
  fire(target,'pointerup',to.x,to.y,0);
  fire(target,'mouseup',to.x,to.y,0);
}
```
- For Lichess, chessground uses `pointerdown` and `pointermove` on the board, with pointer capture. Synthetic `setPointerCapture` may throw for untrusted pointer? Chessground may call it; in Chrome, `setPointerCapture` requires an active pointer (trusted). It might throw and break the handler. For Lichess, click-click is supported, so use click mode first. Drag fallback may fail similarly; fine.
- For chess.com, drag fallback likely requires trusted pointer capture too; warn.

Promotion:
```js
function findPromotionChoice(pieceName, color) {
  var containers = document.querySelectorAll('.promotion, .promotion-window, .promotion-menu, [class*="promotion"]');
  for each container:
    if (!isShown(container)) continue;
    var rect = container.getBoundingClientRect(); if (rect.width*rect.height > 400*400) continue;
    var nodes = container.querySelectorAll('piece, .promotion-piece, [data-piece], button, .piece, [class*="queen"], [class*="rook"], ...');
    ...
}
```
Need to avoid `[class*="queen"]` matching the board's queen if the container is the whole page due to `[class*="promotion"]` matching a wrapper. Restrict to containers whose class includes promotion and max size 500x500, and visible. Then inside, find candidates.
- Candidate matching:
  - `data-piece` value: q/queen/wq/bq/5? Normalize lower.
  - class text includes pieceName (queen) OR the 1-letter code `wq`/`bq`.
  - For Lichess, `piece.queen` (no color).
  - For chess.com, `promotion-piece wq`.
  - Exclude candidates that are the whole dialog.
  - If color is known, prefer candidates with the color class/word; if none, accept any piece matching the name.
- Sort:
  - exact color + piece → 0
  - piece only → 1
- Click candidate:
```js
var r = candidate.getBoundingClientRect();
await clickPoint(candidate, r.left+r.width/2, r.top+r.height/2);
```
- If clickPoint uses elementFromPoint and the dialog is on top, returns candidate. Good.
- If no candidate, try `container.querySelector('[data-piece="q"]')` etc. Include a broader query list.
- If no dialog found within 1s, return false. Some sites auto-queen; fine.
- Promotion piece mapping from move.promotion char; default q. Color from opts.color.

`play`:
```js
AutoMover.prototype.play = async function (boardEl, orientation, move, opts) {
  opts = opts || {};
  var rect = boardEl.getBoundingClientRect();
  if (!rect || rect.width < 60) throw new Error('Доска не видна');
  var from = core.squareCenter(move.from, rect, orientation);
  var to = core.squareCenter(move.to, rect, orientation);
  if (opts.mode === 'drag') await drag(boardEl, from, to);
  else {
    await clickPoint(boardEl, from.x, from.y);
    await sleep(90);
    await clickPoint(boardEl, to.x, to.y);
  }
  if (move.promotion) {
    await sleep(300);
    var chosen = await choosePromotion(move.promotion, opts.color, 1200);
    if (!chosen) { await sleep(200); await choosePromotion(move.promotion, opts.color, 600); }
  }
};
```
- For click mode, use boardEl as fallback; `clickPoint(boardEl, x,y)` internally uses elementFromPoint.
- If the board is scrolled partly offscreen, the coordinates might be outside the viewport; `document.elementFromPoint` returns null; fallback boardEl. Events with out-of-viewport coords may be ignored. Could scroll into view in content before. Add `ensureVisible(boardEl)`:
```js
var r = boardEl.getBoundingClientRect();
if (r.top < 0 || r.left < 0 || r.bottom > innerHeight || r.right > innerWidth) {
  boardEl.scrollIntoView({block:'center', inline:'center'});
  await sleep(120);
  rect = boardEl.getBoundingClientRect();
}
```
- But scrolling the board on a game page could move the page; that's okay. Do it only if needed.
- `scrollIntoView` might be intercepted by smooth scrolling; use `{behavior:'instant'}`? Standard options; try. Wait then recompute. Use `block:'center'`.
- After scrolling, the overlay syncs on window scroll. Good.

Let's write automove.js.

