```
- If `doAutoMove` is called from a timer while the board changed (e.g., the opponent moved? It's our turn; no), the re-read check aborts.
- `waitForBoardChange(prevBoard, timeout)`:
```js
function waitForBoardChange(prevBoard, timeoutMs) {
  return new Promise(function(resolve){
    var start = Date.now();
    function check() {
      if (!state.boardEl || !state.adapter) { resolve(false); return; }
      var r = null;
      try { r = state.adapter.read(state.boardEl); } catch (e) {}
