- If the engine is still searching the old position, the new request will supersede; but if we haven't requested yet, the old search might send a bestmove with an old FEN; content ignores. Fine. Could call `state.engine.stop()` when the board is replaced. Do it? If the new board is loading and no request yet, stopping frees CPU. Call stop in initBoard. But if the same board element is re-found after a transient `findBoard` null, we reset and stop; okay. Add `state.engine.stop()`.

